square-body and pyramid-cap kit for the owner-adopted 1812 prototype. Whistler explicitly says the cupolas were not yet built in 1808; occurrence on the selected 1812 date and every kit dimension remain reconstructed. The measured plans and existing lower geometry stay intact. The held Currey comparison shows both formerly missing fittings, while the whole-fort verdict remains DIFFERS. A one-line renderer fix also handles intentionally empty transport roots during detail changes without logging a Three object error.\n\nTicket: T-3041 (parent T-2387). Both remain open and partial.\n\nValidation: stock Ubuntu 26 / Blender 4.5.3 genuinely built only the two MASTERs and two WEBs, then passed all 1,161 source checks before b1d63be1. Independent native/decoded-WEB review preserves lower geometry except UV repacking, 1,033 foreign registry rows, 1,032 available tracked foreign pairs and all six versions. The inherited cupola box winding is inward with consistent normals and DoubleSide materials; no blanket outward-face claim is made. Current e803 integration passes official Liberties/SourceUse owners, full-dataset validation (1,035 fresh assets, zero stale; six fresh versions), strict confidence and existing actual scene-bridge lifecycle/interaction tests.\n\nStill pending: actual current desktop and phone body/Design/Sources checks for both blockhouses, root pixel review and the final current eight-part gate. This PR stays draft and auto-merge is off until those qualify.\n\nPreserved failures: the stock workflow's later browser matrix closed with 7 passes, 10 failures and 1 cancelled leg; its child PR and release jobs were skipped. Those failures are not relabelled PASS. A separate real fresh-browser control of the untouched e803 dev publication measures 39.696 MB against the unchanged 39.600 MB boot budget, versus 39.695 MB in the stock checkpoint. This establishes an existing baseline budget breach, not a waiver or an explanation of the other detail-cost, shadow, batch/